We can see a call to gets, which is vulnerable to a buffer overflow.
Our goal is to redirect execution to the run function, since it calls system("/bin/sh").

To do that, we need to find the correct offset to overwrite EIP.
I used this website to generate a cyclic pattern:
[wiremask](https://wiremask.eu/tools/buffer-overflow-pattern-generator/)
```bash
level1@RainFall:~$ gdb level1
